needs12.csv had the header „სახელი, პროფესია" with 1–12 under „სახელი". A
header that names the name column won outright, so every row was called
„1"…„12": the owner's five electricians were never found, all twelve rows
went „no route", and the list Excel said „nobody" and nothing else — the
BE fault in 50656. The header now wins only over a column that is not a
count; otherwise the first non-count column names the rows, as 3897 meant.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
